---
globs: apps/web/**/*.ts, apps/web/**/*.html, apps/web/**/*.css
alwaysApply: false
---

# Angular (apps/web)

- Standalone components only. Do not write `standalone: true`.
- Use `input()`, `output()`, `model()` — never `@Input` / `@Output`.
- Derived state: `computed`. Use `effect` only to sync with the outside world (DOM APIs, storage, logging).

```ts
// bad — effect writing into a signal
effect(() => this.total.set(this.a() + this.b()));

// good
readonly total = computed(() => this.a() + this.b());
```

- Prefer `inject()` over constructor injection.
- Templates: `@if` / `@for` (with `track`) / `@switch` only. Lazy-load heavy blocks with `@defer`.
- OnPush is the default (D-10). Omit `changeDetection`. Never set `Eager` or `Default`.
- Zoneless (D-10): no `zone.js`, no `NgZone`, no `provideZonelessChangeDetection()`, no packages that require zone.js.

```ts
// bad — "enabling" zoneless that is already the default
providers: [provideZonelessChangeDetection()]
```

- Forms: Signal Forms (`form()` from `@angular/forms/signals`). No Reactive Forms, no template-driven forms.
- Async data: `resource` / `httpResource`.
- SSR-safe: touch `window` / `document` only inside `afterNextRender`.

```ts
// bad
private readonly width = window.innerWidth;

// good
constructor() {
  afterNextRender(() => {
    this.width.set(window.innerWidth);
  });
}
```

- Styling (D-11): Tailwind via plain CSS (`@theme`). No `tailwind.config.js`, no SCSS. Mobile-first (base styles, then `sm:` / `md:`).
- i18n library is still Open (D-09) — do not introduce one here.
